B.aw8=new A.d6("source_heat","Heat","The character gains their power through a slowly growing process, like a steam engine, or channeling spirit, or eating a big sandwich. Whenever you use an ability of this source, you gain 1 heat up to {Power + 1} and then do the ability using your heat as the source. When you would gain a heat but are at the max, instead you gain an overheat effect, and after you perform the ability, set your heat to 0. You pick the overheat effect when you pick the feature. Each overheat effect is a separate source. Features of the same overheat effect share heat, and you track each overheat effects heat levels separately.","During a situation, before making a roll you may warm up making the check with a -1 to the results. After warming up, for the rest of the situation you make that skill check with a +1 to results.","Start the next situation at {Half Power} heat.","The first time you would overheat in the next situation, instead set your heat to {Half Power}.","{1}",B.uI,"epic_source_heat",!1,null,"{Power + 1}",B.ahg,B.a0,null)
B.uH=new A.p8(1,"resource")
B.awb=new A.d6("source_intuitive_magic","Intuitive Magic","The caster can freely cast their magic. You require an implement to use this source. They have {2 * Power * points} Max MP that they regain at the start of each Story. When they use a feature they must spend at least 1 MP and may spend up to {Power + 1} MP using a feature as the Source Value. On problems with an attack or status check, you pay only 1 MP.\nOvercasting: You may push the limits of your magic and spend {Power + Half Power} MP. When you do, if you get problems, you lose {Vitality d6} health which can't be shielded or resisted.","You may spend 2 MP to gain advantage on a skill or defense check. If multiple allies are making the same check, you may spend 1 MP per ally to give them advantage.","Regain {Power * points / 4} MP.","-1 on checks made from Intuitive Magic abilities, and on problems, instead pay the full amount of MP.","1",B.uH,"epic_source_intuitive_magic",!0,"MP","{2 * Power * points}",B.a0,B.a0,null)
B.awd=new A.d6("source_prepared_magic","Prepared Magic","The caster can only cast magic that they have prepared in advance. You require an implement to use this source. They have {2 * Power * points} Max MP and start every Story with Full MP. Whenever they gain points of features, they may pick an equal number of points of features to form their spellbook. After each encounter, the character may prepare uses of their Prepared Magic features, choosing features with the source and features in their spellbook and the amount of MP spent to Prepare the Spell. Each prepared spell uses the MP spent as the Source value. Prepared spells must spend at least 1 MP, and no more than {1+Power} MP. You may prepare as many uses of any features in your spellbook that you can pay for. You may prepare the same feature multiple times.","You may have up to a total of {points} prepared skill spells per story. For each preparation, pick a skill; you may change what you have prepared at the end of a situation. When you perform a skill check, you may use a prepared skill to gain advantage. Your prepared skill spells are objects you can give to your allies to use as well.","Regain {Power * points / 4} MP.","-1 on checks made from Prepared Magic abilities, and on problems, instead pay the full amount of MP.","MP Spent",B.uH,"epic_source_prepared_magic",!0,"MP","{2 * Power * points}",B.a0,B.a0,null)
B.js=new A.p8(2,"resourceWithSelection")
B.awO=new A.bP("Flow","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki point to Ready, Run or Retreat after the ability.",B.a0,!1)
B.awA=new A.bP("Flurry","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki Point to make 1 Melee Attack targeting an enemy range 1. On success, deal {Power d6}. Choose the defense targeted when you pick this.",B.a0,!1)
B.awE=new A.bP("Restore","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki Point to gain {Half Level d12} Regeneration.",B.a0,!1)
B.ax4=new A.bP("Breath","Before you would make an Int, Wis, or Cha defense, you may pay 1 Ki to gain advantage on the roll.",B.a0,!1)
